# QIF artifacts that are GENERATED and HEAVY.
#
# tools/fws_qif_dse.py writes one full `fws_atlas/1` document per Pareto-front
# point under <output_dir>/points/ (D33: the frontier is the atlas entry and the
# clicked point binds the page, so every clickable point needs its own map).
# Each document is a complete placed-and-priced inventory - chips, macros,
# tiles, links, metrics - so a single front costs megabytes and a regenerated
# sweep rewrites all of them.
#
# The dse_report.json/.md beside them ARE checked in: they are the curve. The
# per-point maps are rebuilt by re-running the sweep, and every one of them
# carries the run id of the report it belongs to, so a stale checkout cannot
# silently mix generations.
dse/*/points/
